The shared interactive next-launch digital editor now opens from local
settings when a writable control store is available. It uses keyboard
selection and capture for physical keys and mouse or controller buttons;
touch slots are selected by keyboard. It displays the admitted binding
and the save or rejection outcome. Running mappings are unchanged until
relaunch. Inline regressions cover conflict rejection, capture cancellation,
controller proposals, release of held logical actions, and preservation of
the suspended session and saved profile.

On 2026-11-25 two visible Xvfb/X11 software OpenGL runs exercised the
authored release executable with disposable settings and the configured
shared assets. One rejected a duplicate keyboard assignment without
creating a save, saved a new right-movement key, cancelled a second
capture without modifying the save, and resumed the suspended game.
All 266 measured gameplay submissions met the 16.667 ms work budget.
The other saved a new primary mouse button, swapped the primary and
secondary touch slots, and edited a keyboard assignment while retaining
the earlier changes. Both isolated saved profiles passed the hidden
touch-enabled relaunch smoke, with 444 camera columns, two cooperative
pose families, six reinforcement meters, 600 movement and 20 combat
