Controller-only and touch-only editor navigation, analogue editing,
actual physical devices and audible output remain unverified.

The editor also accepts fixed gamepad navigation independent of the
active gameplay profile: D-pad selects player/action, right shoulder
cycles source, south confirms and east cancels. Controller capture now
reviews the selected physical button before saving; all button identities,
including navigation buttons, remain assignable. Only assigned local
controllers can navigate or capture. Closing the editor routes a single
local pause edge even when that physical button has another gameplay
binding. Modal capture releases existing holds without submitting new
gameplay presses or releases. Synthetic editor and title integration
regressions verify the navigation, cancel/confirm flow and reserved-seat
close routing. Physical controller hardware acceptance remains open.

The interactive editor now accepts the active touch panel's logical
buttons as explicit menu commands. Arrows select the station, action
or pending touch slot; B cycles the family, A starts or confirms
capture, Start clears an optional binding and Pause cancels or exits.
The displayed hints match these commands even when touch slots have
been remapped. Shared editor tests verify touch selection, cancellation,
confirmation and separation from raw controller capture. Title routing
tests exercise all eight commands through the actual remapped panel
geometry, with no gameplay edges on taps, motion or release. The
existing fixed panel atlas budget is retained. Physical touchscreen
and analogue editing acceptance remain open.

The shared next-launch editor also supports signed controller axes.
The axis-specific mode stages negative and positive logical actions
and both hysteresis thresholds as one candidate. Triggers cannot
select a negative action; the ordered thresholds remain within the
admitted signed range. Up/Down selects the physical axis, then the
draft field after confirmation; Left/Right adjusts its value, and
confirmation saves all four fields together. Cancel, focus loss and
controller removal discard the draft. Both digital and axis edits
use the same atomic persistence and title admission path.

A visible virtual X11/OpenGL release run on 2026-11-25 selected the
first station's Right X axis, assigned left/right actions and adjusted
press/release to 17000/9000. No settings file appeared before the
confirmation. The confirmed full profile contained the expected
axis records; a subsequent cancelled edit left its SHA-256 unchanged.
The profile passed a touch-enabled hidden relaunch smoke with 444
camera columns, two cooperative pose families, six reinforcement
meters, 600 movement and 20 combat submissions, and zero movement
work-budget misses. Its saved hash remained unchanged. This verifies
keyboard-driven axis editing and persistence, not physical analogue
controller operation or audible output.

